#
# NOTE: This file contains a top-level Eagle script that will be automatically
#       evaluated by the [hotkey autoload] sub-command.  The actual evaluation
#       will take place in a "safe" interpreter with a very limited subset of
#       commands.  Access to the [hotkey add] sub-command by this script will
#       be allowed; however, access to all other sub-commands of the [hotkey]
#       command will be denied.  If there are any per-user, per-machine, or
#       per-domain files containing configured hot-keys that should be loaded
#       by the [hotkey autoload] sub-command, they should be named as follows:
#
#       hotkey-autoload-${USER}.eagle
#       hotkey-autoload-${MACHINE}.eagle
#       hotkey-autoload-${DOMAIN}.eagle
#       hotkey-autoload.eagle
#
#       Whenever the [hotkey autoload] sub-command is executed, if any of the
#       above named files exist in the current directory, an attempt will be
#       made to evaluate them [in a "safe" interpreter], in exactly the order
#       listed above.
#
hotkey add F13 LogSynchronous {puts stdout "This is a test hot-key."}
